{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/none"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/equal(using:)","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/full(using:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BackoffJitter"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Jitter takes a nominal wait and picks the wait to use instead. It works on any clock’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Duration"},{"type":"text","text":", and the operators that wait take it as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jitter:"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/ExponentialBackoffStrategy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (each backoff delay), "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/TimerSequence","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each tick falls inside its period) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"delay"},{"type":"text","text":" on units of work and sequences (each wait)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds follow “Exponential Backoff and Jitter” (AWS Architecture Blog):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/none","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the nominal wait, exactly."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/full(using:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": anywhere from zero up to the nominal wait."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/equal(using:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": half the nominal wait, plus anywhere up to the other half."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": at least the nominal wait, and up to three times the previous wait","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this jitter produced, so the waits spread further apart the longer they go on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each random kind draws from the generator it was given, one value per wait, so a seeded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generator makes the waits reproducible. A jitter value holds its generator, and for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/decorrelated(using:)"},{"type":"text","text":" the previous wait, by reference: copies of a value share them, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do the operators it is passed to. Make a new value for each operator that should have its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let backoff = ExponentialBackoffStrategy(base: 2, maxDelay: .seconds(60), jitter: .equal())","let heartbeat = TimerSequence.publish(every: .seconds(30), jitter: .full())"]}],"kind":"content"}],"ident